{"name":"Romantic Holiday","hex":"#a497a1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"romantic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a work of literature, a writer etc.: being like or having the characteristics of a romance, or poetic tale of a mythic or quasi-historical time; fantastic. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Fictitious, imaginary."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person with romantic character (a character like those of the knights in a mythic romance).","A person who is behaving romantically (in a manner befitting someone who feels an idealized form of love)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/romantic"},{"term":"holiday","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A day on which a religious event or secular celebration is traditionally observed.","A day declared free from work by the state or government."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take a period of time away from work or study.","To spend a period of time in recreational travel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holiday"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holiday","blocks":[{"text":"A holiday is a day or other period of time set aside for festivals or recreation. Public holidays are set by public authorities and vary by state or region. Religious holidays are set by religious organizations for their members and are often also observed as public holidays in religious majority countries. Some religious holidays, such as Christmas, have become secularised by part or all of those who observe them. In addition to secularisation, many holidays have become commercialised due to the growth of industry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Lathmar_Holi_2022_in_Nandgaon%2C_Uttar_Pradesh_%28edited%29.jpg/330px-Lathmar_Holi_2022_in_Nandgaon%2C_Uttar_Pradesh_%28edited%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holiday","wikidata":"Q1445650"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/500px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/1280px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg/500px-Champs-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChamps-Elysees_Bastille_Day_2013_Paris_t090858.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/500px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/1280px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg/500px-School_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchool_Children_On_a_Mission.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Eid_Mubarak_2012_%287877275396%29.jpg/500px-Eid_Mubarak_2012_%287877275396%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Eid_Mubarak_2012_%287877275396%29.jpg/1280px-Eid_Mubarak_2012_%287877275396%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thum